{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3200-76cd-b849-54792dd695d9","id":"01a1a64f-fe87-771c-86b0-5b8acb85e3a3","idempotency_key":"27f7c78d447d197170cde66b6ff3854e755e73739b6295cc46c12ff3f11178ad","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:27:02Z","payload":{"note":"4 of 5. The tools existed as SPECS ONLY: tools/list advertised add_chapter, add_board_to_chapter, reorder_chapters, write_study_text, publish_study and get_chapter, and the host answered 'no tool called X' to every one - which is worse than not listing them, because a client has no way to know before it tries. All six are implemented now, and one test walks the registry asserting no SessionWrite tool is advertised-but-unimplemented so this cannot silently return. Published studies refuse writes with a conflict naming the version and saying to make a copy; the first guard I wrote used current_version > 0 and was wrong, because adding a chapter bumps the version, so a new study looked published after its first chapter - the lifecycle field is the real signal. Two more corrections came from the tests: Db::write_study_text did not exist (added, over study_chapters - the table is not called 'chapters'), and add_board_to_chapter creates a board from title/fen rather than linking an existing id. LEFT OPEN: i-4697 is gated on t-5638 by the ticket's own dependency, and the tool refuses the tick; the work it describes is done, so it needs the editor ticket to land before it can be closed honestly.","target":"t-bb8b"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
